{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Proven root cause: a transient GitHub `git fetch` hang becomes a durable `LLM-Review -1` that suppresses its own backfill recovery\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGerrit changes 1189 PS1, 1193 PS1 and 1208 PS1 (7 in journald since 2026-07-31) carry\n`[LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (review-error)]`. The `-1` is spurious: 1189 and 1193\nflipped to `+1` on re-review against effectively identical code. Because the review bot's\nbackfill reconciler only re-drives changes that have NO `LLM-Review` vote, the spurious `-1`\nremoves the change from its own safety net, so a several-second network blip permanently\nwedges a contributor's change until a maintainer re-triggers by hand.\n\n## Proven mechanism (reproduced; each step cited)\n\n1. Per review the bot makes a throwaway clone (`voter.py:603` `TemporaryDirectory`;\n   `gerrit_client.py:314 clone_change_ref`) whose `origin` is the **GitHub mirror**\n   (`gerrit_client.py:359`).\n2. The attested gate calls `materialize_tickets` -> `resolve_ref(..., blobless=False)` ->\n   `_fetch_origin` -> `git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin`\n   (`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:337-393`).\n3. **That fetch intermittently hangs.** Reproduced inside `compose-review-bot-1`: 25\n   consecutive runs of the exact command, **2 hung past 320s (rc=124)**, the other 23\n   finished in 1-3s. Median 2s; the repo is 80 MB / 54k objects — a connection stall, not a\n   large transfer and not load.\n4. git has no `http.lowSpeedLimit`/`lowSpeedTime` configured, so the stall burns the whole\n   `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 300` (`repo_snapshot.py:295`) and `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` is converted\n   to `SnapshotFetchError` at `repo_snapshot.py:376-380`. **Verified in this session** by\n   forcing `subprocess.run` inside `repo_snapshot` to raise `TimeoutExpired`:\n   `_fetch_origin` raised `SnapshotFetchError: git fetch from 'origin' timed out after 300s\n   (attested mode fails closed)`.\n5. `adapter.code_review_decision`'s blanket `except Exception` (`adapter.py:207-211`) cannot\n   tell an *infrastructure* fault from a *review* fault, so it returns\n   `_block(\"review-error\", {})`. **Verified in this session**: raising `SnapshotFetchError`\n   out of `produce_code_review_verdict` yields\n   `decision=BLOCK, coverage_gap=True, message=\"[LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (review-error)]\"`.\n6. The voter maps that BLOCK to `cfg.llm_review_block_value` and POSTs it\n   (`voter.py:673-680`). **Verified in this session**: `review_and_vote` returned\n   `status=\"voted\"` with a `-1` POSTed to the fake Gerrit, and recorded the dedup row.\n7. **The vote suppresses the designed safety net.** `reconcile.py:205-211` pre-filters on\n   `store.already_voted(...)` and `gc.has_llm_review_vote(...)` and `continue`s, so backfill\n   only re-reviews *vote-less* changes. Posting the `-1` therefore removes the change from\n   backfill permanently.\n\nEvery timeout timestamp in journald is EXACTLY a vote timestamp (23:39:03 ch1189,\n00:22:11 ch1193, 04:46:53, 16:41:48 ch1208). Normal review setup is 14-19s; the failures are\na step-function to 300s.\n\nThe inner `_GIT_TIMEOUT` (300s) always fires before the outer `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`\n(1200s, `review_bot/config.py:30`), so an infra stall is structurally guaranteed to take the\nvote-bearing path and never the benign no-vote path that `app.py:161-176` and\n`reconcile.py:222-226` already implement for a hung review.\n\n## Alternatives ruled out by evidence\n\n* **\"transfer too large\"** (the error string's own guess) — REFUTED: 80 MB repo, median 2s.\n* **Auto-deploy restarting the bot mid-review** — REFUTED. `compose-review-bot-1` recreation\n  times were 23:25:04, 00:00:22, 03:59:28, 05:37:03 UTC; each of the four timeouts falls\n  strictly inside a single container's lifetime (1208's container had been up 12h). A SIGTERM\n  would not emit this log line, and the same container kept reviewing afterwards.\n* **CPU / credit starvation** — REFUTED: `CPUCreditBalance` flat at ~864.\n* **Disk pressure** — REFUTED: root 61% used, /var/gerrit 9%.\n* **Diff-dependent** — REFUTED: reproduced with no review running.\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the review bot distinguish a *retryable infrastructure fault* from a *review\nconclusion*, and route only the former to the existing, already-tested no-vote path. This\nfits because the system already has the correct behaviour for this class one layer up\n(`app.py:161-176`, `reconcile.py:222-226`: abandon without voting, let backfill retry) — the\ndefect is that the inner layer is inconsistent with it, not that a new mechanism is needed.\nFixing the inner layer to match the outer one is the smallest change that restores\nself-healing, and it adds no new subsystem, config key, or abstraction.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py`** — add a narrow classifier\n   `_is_retryable_infra(exc)` that matches `rebar._snapshot.SnapshotFetchError`,\n   `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`, builtin `TimeoutError` (which `asyncio.TimeoutError` and\n   `socket.timeout` alias), and builtin `ConnectionError`, walking a bounded `__cause__`\n   chain so a wrapped transport fault is still recognised. When\n   `produce_code_review_verdict` raises such an exception, return a new\n   `{\"decision\": \"ABSTAIN\", ...}` result instead of `_block(\"review-error\", {})`. Every other\n   exception, the gate-import failure, and every genuine verdict path are untouched.\n2. **`src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`** — immediately before the decision→vote mapping at\n   `voter.py:673-680`, handle `decision == \"ABSTAIN\"`: emit the greppable `_voter_error(...)`\n   marker (so `rebar/host:voter_errors` still counts the fault), POST no vote, write no\n   dedup row, and return `{\"status\": \"error\", \"stage\": \"review_infra\"}`. This mirrors the\n   existing `review_setup` early return at `voter.py:663-672`.\n\n`reconcile.py` needs no change: it counts only `status == \"voted\"`, and a change left\nvote-less is re-picked by the `has_llm_review_vote` pre-filter on the next pass. The\nmerge-path `_merge_coverage_gap_decision` (`voter.py:243`) is deliberately left voting as\ntoday — it is a Gerrit REST fault on a change the bot could still reach, and its current\nfail-closed behaviour is pinned by `test_voter_merge_path_rest_failure_votes_block_coverage_gap`.\n\nAcceptance criterion 5 (configure `http.lowSpeedLimit`/`lowSpeedTime` so the stall aborts in\nseconds) is out of scope here and is filed as a separate child ticket; this ticket removes\nthe durable damage, that one shortens the stall.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py` — the classifier, the `ABSTAIN` result, and the branch in\n  the `except` at `adapter.py:207-211`.\n* `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` — the `ABSTAIN` early return before the vote mapping.\n* `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` — the unit tests below (the existing home of every\n  `adapter` / `voter` / `reconcile` unit test).\n\nNo other file changes. No config key, no new module, no dependency.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded to `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`, using the existing `FakeGerrit` / `DedupStore` /\n`_cfg` / `_event` / `ReconcileGerrit` harness (no network):\n\n* **Happy path (the bug):** `produce_code_review_verdict` raises `SnapshotFetchError` ->\n  `adapter.code_review_decision` returns `decision == \"ABSTAIN\"`, and\n  `voter.review_and_vote` POSTs **no** vote (`FakeGerrit.votes == []`) and writes **no**\n  dedup row.\n* **Failure/contrast path (no silent-pass hole):** an ordinary `RuntimeError` from\n  `produce_code_review_verdict` still returns `BLOCK` and the voter still POSTs the `-1`;\n  a genuine blocking finding still POSTs the `-1`. An `ABSTAIN` never POSTs a `+1`.\n* **Backfill re-eligibility:** after an abstained review, `reconcile.once` with a\n  `has_llm_review_vote`-honest fake re-drives the same change on the next pass (it is a\n  candidate again), whereas the pre-fix `-1` made it skip.\n* **Degraded-mode safety:** with the events-log erroring (`RECONCILE_DEGRADED`), an\n  abstained change stays unvoted, so it is unsubmittable — \"don't vote\" cannot create a pass.\n* **Mutation check:** the new tests are run against the reverted fix to confirm they go RED,\n  and against the fix to confirm GREEN.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A retryable infrastructure failure raised out of `produce_code_review_verdict` — at\n      minimum `SnapshotFetchError`, plus `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`, `TimeoutError` and\n      `ConnectionError` — results in **no `LLM-Review` vote** and **no dedup row**. Checked\n      by a unit test asserting `FakeGerrit.votes == []` and\n      `DedupStore.already_voted(...) is False`.\n- [ ] A `VOTER_ERROR` marker is still emitted on that path so `rebar/host:voter_errors`\n      counts it. Checked by a unit test asserting the `VOTER_ERROR` line reaches stderr\n      (`capsys`) with the change id.\n- [ ] A genuine review conclusion still votes fail-closed exactly as today: a real blocking\n      finding, an INDETERMINATE, a scanner abstain, a gate-disabled verdict and a\n      non-retryable exception all still POST the block value. Checked by the existing\n      adapter/voter tests continuing to pass unmodified plus one new contrast test for the\n      non-retryable exception.\n- [ ] Nothing provisional is posted on an abstained change (no `+1`, no `-1`, no message), so\n      backfill is not re-suppressed. Checked by the same `votes == []` assertion.\n- [ ] An abstained change is re-picked by the backfill reconciler on a later pass. Checked by\n      a `reconcile.once` unit test that reviews the change again once no vote is present.\n- [ ] Degraded mode is safe: with the events-log unavailable an unvoted change stays unvoted\n      and therefore unsubmittable. Checked by a unit test asserting no vote is cast in the\n      degraded path.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and\n      `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` all exit 0.\n\n## Relationship to other tickets\n\n* `bb9b-608f-0183-4ca5` (contributor-triggerable re-review) — this root cause is the dominant\n  *source* of the fail-closed `-1`s that story exists to let contributors clear. Fixing this\n  shrinks that story's load; it does not replace it.\n* `0347-b2cc-e6e9-4f6b` — filed on the auto-deploy hypothesis, which this bug REFUTES with\n  on-box container-lifetime evidence. Its second half (\"fail-NO-VOTE instead of fail-closed\n  for retryable conditions\") is the correct fix and is subsumed here.\n* NOT related to bug `d5c7-0d57-c3ab-4e93` (plan-review Pass-2 verification-index rejection):\n  that is a deterministic LLM output-validation fault with no network involved. This fault\n  makes zero LLM calls — it dies in git before the first prompt."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785705617026795001,"uuid":"f363d897-44a8-4abf-9dfd-18829b5fb07d"}